# Public keys that can decrypt deploy/secrets.env.age. One age recipient per line; lines
# starting with # are comments. These are PUBLIC keys — safe to commit; the private halves
# never enter the repo (secrets.sh header).
#
# encrypt_stdin re-encrypts to THIS list on every `secrets.sh set` and `import`, so a
# recipient added here survives re-encryption. A recipient added any other way is stripped
# by the next write (SECRETS_PROGRAM.md 3.7). The escrow/break-glass recipient from action
# S1 belongs here, added in the same commit that escrows its private half.
#
# founder laptop — ~/.config/prospector/age-key.txt
